This paper investigates the normalized ground state solution for the given biharmonic Choquard type equation \begin{align*}
  \begin{split}
  \left\{
  \begin{array}{ll}
  \Delta^2u-\Delta u+\mu u+\lambda f(u)=|x|^\lambda u^p, \quad \text{in}\ \ \mathbb{R}^3,
  \end{array}
  \right.
  \end{split}
  \end{align*} under specific constraints and finds a normalized ground state solution using a carefully constructed minimization process in an appropriate Sobolev space.
